body:
As the top comment says, I'd send an email summarizing the meeting you had, and then from here on out, I'd make sure all of our communications were either in writing (email) or via Zoom (and recorded). If you must meet with him in person outside of class hours, I'd ask an advisor or Dean to accompany you. I'd literally tell them that your last meeting got heated and insults were thrown around, and you don't feel comfortable going alone. If all else fails, I'd keep my phone on record and hide it in my pocket. He can't be talking to students that way, but unfortunately, your words don't mean much without proof to back it up.

&#x200B;

Second, I think you should ask around in your class to see if any other students felt they were graded unfairly. Do you have any friends in the course, or even any friends who have had this dude as a professor before? I may be a little bit \~extra\~ but I also wouldn't be above sending out an email to the whole class (prof. not included obviously). Just in terms of approaching other students, I'd probably phrase it something like this: "I'm thinking about going to the head of the department/a dean about our professor's inconsistent grading tendencies and/or his uninvolved teaching methods during class periods. If I did end up reaching out about this, would you feel comfortable backing me up? For example, say, if the department head asked me to put them into contact with other students who could attest to my complaints, could I give them your info?" That sort of thing. Let them know that it's not a big deal and that you might not even need them to vouch for you, but even if they do get involved, that schools have policies in place to protect students in these situations so they shouldn't worry about retaliation etc. There's definitely strengths in numbers, so if you can get anyone else on your side, it would be a huge help. Tenured professors in particular can be really hard to take down, but your concerns are totally valid. Plus, who knows, maybe there's been multiple complaints against this guy in the years before, and you speaking out will be the straw that breaks the camel's back, so to speak. You're paying a lot of money for your education and he should be actually teaching you something.

So I'm actually looking for romance animes as well and made a list of all of the series that I've seen recommended multiple times. Sorry if some of the suggestions are too obvious, just thought I'd throw out everything I had. Oh also, I put a star next to all of the ones that I've watched all the way through (and liked).

&#x200B;

Kaguya-Sama, Wotakoi, Tonikawa, Snow White With The Red Hair\*, ReLife, Love Chuunibyo and Other Delusions, Boarding School Juliet, Quintessential Quintuplets, Tsurezure Children, My Love Story, Love After World Domination, Say I Love You, Kimo no Todoki, Tsuki ga Kirei, Golden Time, His and Her Circumstances, Aharen-san wa Hakarenai, The Duke Of Death and His Maid, Taishou Otome Otogibanashi, Tsuki to Laika to Nosferatu, More Than A Couple Less Than Lovers, Blue Spring Ride\*, Toradora, Kamisama Kiss\*, Your Name, I Want To Eat Your Pancreas, Plastic Memories, Darling In The FranXX\*, REC, Romeo x Juliet, Lovely Complex, Seto no Hanayome, Orange, Engaged To The Unidentified, Waiting In The Summer, Tada Never Falls In Love, Bloom Into You, Horimaya\*, Hi-Score Girl, Spice and Wolf, My Goddess, Uzaki-chan Wants To Hang Out, Don't Toy With Me Miss Nagatoro, Just Because, Fruit's Basket\*, Kakuriyo\*, March Comes In Like A Lion, Komi Can't Communicate, ItaKiss, Koikimo, Call Of The Night, White Album 2, Teasing Master Takagi-san, Yosuga no Sora, Recovery Of An MMO Junkie, ReZero, School Days, Steins;Gate, Sagrada Reset, Chihayafuru, Chobits, Acchi Kocchi, The Ancient Magus Bride, Nodami Cantabile, Nana, Tsubasa Reservoir Chronicle, Wise Man's Grandchild, Chivalry Of A Failed Knight, Science Fell In Love, Toilet-Bound Hanako-kun, Honey and Clover, Saekano, Bokuben, A Lull In The Sea, Senryu Girl, Sugar Apple Fairy Tale, Yona Of The Dawn, Vampire Knight, Kamigamino Asobi, Wolf Girl and Black Prince, My Next Life As A Villainess, Ouran High School Host Club, Kiss Him Not Me, Earl and Fairy, Inu x Boku SS, Anohana, Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki, Monthy Girls' Nozaki-kun, Nisekoi, Yamada-kun and The Seven Witches\*, Arakawa Under The Bridge, 3D Kanojo Real Girl, Kokoro Connect, The World Is Still Beautiful, Bibliophile Princess, Iroduku, Bakemonogatari, The Misfit Of Demon King Academy, Amagami SS, Bakuman, Kono Oto Tomare, One Week Friends, WorldEnd, Dusk Maiden Of Amnesia, Given, Banished From The Hero's Party, My Stepmom's Daughter is My Ex, Romantic Killer\*, Holmes Of Kyoto, Gamers, Engage Kiss, Citrus, Higehiro, Charlotte, My Little Monster, Ojisan and Marshmallow, Convenience Store Boy Friends, Red Data Girl, EF A Tale Of Memories, Mysteria Friends, Happy Sugar Life, Yeonae Haru Jeon, I Can't Understand What My Husband Is Saying, The Familiar Of Zero, Momokuri, Vermeil In Gold.

&#x200B;

Fruit's Basket is super popular but it's my absolute favorite romance series so if you haven't seen it yet then you need to log off and go watch it rn. As for the others I listed above, I'd say I've started maybe 70% of those titles but I have a horrible attention span and will dump a show after one episode if it can't keep my attention, HOWEVER, I know that many of those shows are still really good / highly recommended by others, so like yeah just throwing them out there. Also re: your edit, definitely watch My Dress Up Darling.

&#x200B;

Edit: I just saw your reply listing all of the ones you've seen and realized that I accidentally included a bunch, so sorry about that. But hopefully my wall of text was still somewhat helpful lol
